3. Rg5 { cutting off the enemy king - Baburin. } ) 
Kc4 $1 ( { By now an ideal place for the king, where it limits the movements of its white counterpart. Obviously, had White played } 1... Kc4 1. Rg8 { , he could now have chased away the king by } 3. Rg4 ) 
3. Rc8 Rh6+ 4. Kb7 Kb5 $1 5. Rc7 ( { Or } 5. c6 Rg6 6. c7 Rb6 { with a perpetual. } ) 
